### SubjectVersion API Test

@base_url = https://localhost:7141/api
@token = Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Create a new SubjectVersion
POST {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{token}}

{
  "subjectId": 1,
  "versionCode": "1.0",
  "versionName": "First Version",
  "description": "Initial version of the subject",
  "isActive": true,
  "isDefault": true,
  "effectiveFrom": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "effectiveTo": null
}

### 2. Get all SubjectVersions (paginated)
GET {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: {{token}}

### 3. Get SubjectVersions by Subject ID
GET {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/subject/1
Authorization: {{token}}

### 4. Get SubjectVersion by ID
GET {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/1
Authorization: {{token}}

### 5. Get default version for a subject
GET {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/subject/1/default
Authorization: {{token}}

### 6. Get all active versions
GET {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/active
Authorization: {{token}}

### 7. Update a SubjectVersion
PUT {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{token}}

{
  "versionCode": "1.1",
  "versionName": "Updated Version",
  "description": "Updated description",
  "isActive": true,
  "isDefault": true,
  "effectiveFrom": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "effectiveTo": null
}

### 8. Set version as default
POST {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/1/set-default
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{token}}

### 9. Toggle active status
POST {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/1/toggle-active
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{token}}

### 10. Delete a SubjectVersion
DELETE {{base_url}}/SubjectVersion/1
Authorization: {{token}}
